{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/789274-2nd-ed-disciplines-1st-ed-rules","id":789274,"title":"2nd Ed Disciplines, 1st Ed rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-19T09:27:03-08:00","id":789274,"title":"2nd Ed Disciplines, 1st Ed rules?","content":"My group is going to try World of Darkness, specifically a game inspired by Requiem for Rome but set in the waning days of Roman Britain. However, as I begin my prep I've been looking at these forums and at the various rulesets and I'm somewhat torn.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition advantages: Disciplines are much cooler.<br /> <br /> 1st edition advantages: seems simpler, and I own hardcopies of the nWoD and Requiem corebooks (both important as most of the group has never played any WoD before and my experience is extremely limited).<br /> <br /> Is it feasible for me to use the Disciplines from _Blood and Smoke_ but otherwise stick to 1st edition? Or are the discipline changes too tied to the other B&amp;S/God Machine changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10328-bkwrm79","name":"bkwrm79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:05:46-08:00","id":789286,"title":"","content":"It's feasible, but you would have to make some decisions about how things convert over. For instance, would the active form of resilience still negate damage, or would it provide 1st edition style armor? Also, a vampire won't be able to spend 2 Vitae per turn until BP 4, unless you adopt the 2nd edition BP table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:06:26-08:00","id":789288,"title":"","content":"Ought to work for the most part (at least looking at the core Disciplines, not including blood sorcery or coils). A couple things to keep in mind:<ul><li>The mind-affecting Disciplines (Dominate, Majesty and Nightmare) are hooked into the Condition system. Reference the Conditions appendix and integrate the rules for their respective Conditions, including the ability to resolve and end the Condition through certain means. You don't have to use the Condition system itself \u2013 so you don't have to tag a Mesmerized card onto a character or track beats/experience points from them or anything \u2013 but their writeups do contain rules that govern what those Disciplines do.</li> <li>A couple powers can be resisted by vampires via lashing out with the Predatory Aura. That costs Willpower against other vampires and is generally regarded as a hostile, almost violent act, so the opportunity cost isn't the same as vampires just being immune to them, but you may want to take note of them and consider whether to create an alternate recourse if you aren't using the Predatory Aura.</li> <li>The passive and active effects of Vigor on combat rolls are distinct in second edition rules, which distinguish weapon damage from bonus dice, but in first edition terms, adding Vigor to your Strength and also adding Vigor as a weapon bonus just amounts to adding Vigor to your dice pool twice. I'd suggest something else. Perhaps the active use of Vigor could just directly add to damage on a successful hit, effectively applying the 2e weapon rules as an exception case for this power, or it could apply 8-Again to the roll, or something.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:08:28-08:00","id":789290,"title":"","content":"They aren't that compatible without taking into account beats, the way armor work, the way vampires can shrug damage naturally, and another number of things, so I'd recommend sticking to the ruleset that you got, and update later when everyone got access to it. Way less headaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T10:10:30-08:00","id":789293,"title":"","content":"Unless you're playing a mekhet, using your discipline powers effectively requires you to successfully activate a low level power to install a condition on your victim first, making those mechanics from 2nd edition also a requirement. You could ditch that requirement and simply say they successfully generate the desired effect with an activation roll, but you will need to go back and revise/install activation rolls, resist checks, and costs accordingly because undoing/avoiding the conditions are the real key to resisting or shaking off discipline effects, not jacking up your composure or resolve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:18:53-08:00","id":789921,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I think for now I'll try to keep it simple, then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10328-bkwrm79","name":"bkwrm79","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}